{
  "id": 18,
  "title": "SID Steering",
  "briefing": "OSPF normally sends RTR-1 traffic to RTR-5 over the short upper path through RTR-3. Build SR Policy-1 on RTR-1 to steer it over the lower path instead. In the SR tab, set Dest to 10.0.35.2 and enter these comma-separated segments: 2.2.2.2, adj:2.2.2.2:1, 5.5.5.5. The first Node SID reaches RTR-2 along SPF, the adjacency SID forces RTR-2 Gi0/1 toward RTR-4, and the final Node SID carries the packet to RTR-5. Send a packet from RTR-1 to RTR-5 when the policy is ACTIVE.",
